 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Yusuf and his brother are never drawn; no cup, camels or caravan. Wheat for «جهزهم بجهازهم» (the provisions). The caller's «إنكم لسارقون» carries As-Sa'di's «ولعل هذا المؤذن، لم يعلم بحقيقة الحال». STAGING v4: c1 (69) in Yusuf's guest house (Al-Muyassar: his house of hospitality): Yusuf is only a blue drop labelled Yusuf, at the right; his brothers come in (a plain group of three in dark robes) with Binyamin, a single plain man (69:2). On 69:5 (he took his brother to himself) Binyamin walks to Yusuf's side, and Yusuf speaks to him (69:8, 69:13; secretly, Al-Muyassar). No embrace is drawn. c2 (70-72) in the town: the caravan (the brothers and their camel) is furnished (a wheat plate for the provisions, 70:2-3); nothing is drawn while the cup is put in the bag (70:4-8): no cup, no bag, no hand, no Yusuf; the caravan sets off (70:9, both tafsirs: when they had set out) and a single caller appears at the right (70:10, a man in plain robes) and calls to them (70:12). The brothers answer and come back toward him (71:1-4, As-Sa'di: they came toward them to remove the charge); the caller says what is missing (72:1) and promises the reward (72:10), with a wheat plate for the camel load of food (72:8, Al-Muyassar). c3 (73): the brothers swear that they did not come to do harm and shake their heads in denial (73:6). Binyamin is not singled out in the caravan scenes."
 },
